SCOPE (epic vms-da0, F2 "GCC-as-VMS-oracle" — the compiler-proper forcing
function, following F1's GNU as): this vendoring needs GCC's C AND C++ front
ends (cc1, cc1plus) plus the middle end/backend they share with every
language, and the host-side build support libraries (libcpp, libiberty,
libdecnumber, libbacktrace) that `make all-gcc` links into cc1/cc1plus's
driver. C++ is IN scope as of vms-796 (F2a) — NOT a scope-creep choice but a
hard build requirement discovered by vms-0d2's wall-catalog probe: GCC-14's
shared middle end (`gcc/fold-const.cc`) references `EXPR_STMT`, defined only
in `gcc/cp/cp-tree.def`, which is only present/parsed when C++ is a
configured language. There is no C-only subset of `make all-gcc` for GCC 14
— cc1 and cc1plus share too much of the middle end to separate. This
vendoring explicitly still does NOT need: gdb (never shipped in GCC's own
tarball), any OTHER language front end (ada/d/fortran/go/jit/m2/rust/objc++),
the target runtime libraries (libgcc/libstdc++-v3/libgomp/libitm/libatomic/
libquadmath/libsanitizer/libvtv/libobjc/libssp/libphobos/libgo/libgm2/
libgrust/libcc1/libffi — none are needed to build the HOST tools cc1/cc1plus
themselves, only to build target code with them, which this bead does not
reach — libstdc++-v3 in particular is a *link-time* wall for a HOSTED cc1
build, not a build-time need for `make all-gcc` itself), the maintainer/
translation trees (po/, contrib/, maintainer-scripts/), or the DejaGNU test
fixtures (gcc/testsuite/ alone is 469M — never a build dependency of
`make all-gcc`).

